WEBVTT

00:00.440 --> 00:05.170
<i>Today, we've come to the beast knight 
stables, which have lots of rare animals!
</i>

00:05.860 --> 00:09.580
<i>The captain of the Beast Knights Legion
 is supposed to take us around.</i>

00:09.580 --> 00:11.190
<i>I wonder what he's like!</i>

00:12.050 --> 00:14.520
Hey, looks like he's already here.

00:19.680 --> 00:21.770
It's a pleasure to meet you, my lady.

00:21.770 --> 00:24.920
I am the captain of a special squad 
called the Beast Knights Legion.

00:25.250 --> 00:26.620
My name is Lestin Ogma.

00:27.460 --> 00:29.120
Please, call me Les.

00:30.070 --> 00:32.890
<i>Oh, he seems nice and pleasant.</i>

00:33.390 --> 00:35.460
I'm Nefertima Osphe.

00:35.460 --> 00:37.420
Pweased to meet you, Mister Les.

00:37.420 --> 00:39.780
The pleasure is all mine.

00:42.260 --> 00:44.970
<i>So this is Lady Nefertima,
 who I keep hearing about.</i>

00:45.460 --> 00:46.940
<i>She's so ordinary.</i>

00:46.940 --> 00:48.910
I can walk all by myself!

00:48.910 --> 00:50.550
Well, you're gonna wander off!

00:50.550 --> 00:52.040
Nuh-uh!

00:52.040 --> 00:53.220
Yes, you will.

00:52.250 --> 00:56.110
<i>She hardly seems as special as Dan described.</i>

00:53.220 --> 00:54.440
Nuh-uh!

00:54.440 --> 00:55.330
Come on, now.

00:55.330 --> 00:56.290
I won't!

00:59.630 --> 01:02.190
Can you believe it? A dragon...

01:02.190 --> 01:05.790
Ghizel, their leader, no less,
let her ride on his back.

01:06.510 --> 01:08.990
He doesn't even let me do that.

01:09.310 --> 01:14.320
<i>Dan loves dragons so much that he left
the Beast Knights for the Dragon Knights</i>

01:14.320 --> 01:17.100
<i>and even became their captain. 
Yet he's jealous of her?</i>

01:20.770 --> 01:23.220
<i>I see we have a little charmer on our hands.</i>

01:23.580 --> 01:27.030
<i>Very well. I shall accept this challenge.</i>

01:36.780 --> 01:41.700
<b><i>Fluffy Paradise</i></b>

02:58.360 --> 03:03.280
<b><i>Episode 3   A Lovely Gift</i></b>

02:59.270 --> 03:00.270
Now then...

03:00.270 --> 03:02.110
Welcome to the beast stables.

03:02.600 --> 03:04.150
It's so big!

03:04.150 --> 03:06.070
<i>It's like a safari park!</i>

03:06.640 --> 03:11.790
This place is also maintained by magic 
so the animals can live their best lives.

03:13.940 --> 03:15.580
Mister horsey!

03:16.320 --> 03:20.330
While we're at it, why don't we
take a look around from horseback?

03:21.150 --> 03:22.050
Can we really?!

03:29.250 --> 03:32.180
<i>Oh my gosh! He's so cool!</i>

03:32.180 --> 03:35.830
<i>His mane is so silky smooth! 
He's so valiant yet elegant!</i>

03:37.930 --> 03:41.040
This is Uwaz, the leader of the herd.

03:41.960 --> 03:44.870
<i>Yeah, he's definitely giving 
off that boss aura.</i>

03:45.150 --> 03:47.710
I'm Neema! It's a pweasure 
to meet you, Uwaz!

03:50.080 --> 03:52.490
<i>Wh-What was that just now?</i>

03:52.490 --> 03:54.040
<i>Did he just snort at me?</i>

03:55.930 --> 03:58.160
<i>Well, if that's how it's gonna be...</i>

03:58.160 --> 04:01.490
Uwaz! Let's play! Uwaz! Uwaz!

04:03.580 --> 04:06.550
<i>Okay... not really the friendly type.</i>

04:06.790 --> 04:09.460
I do apologize, Lady Nefertima.

04:09.460 --> 04:12.510
Uwaz can be a bit selfish...

04:14.320 --> 04:14.820
Huh?

04:15.060 --> 04:18.510
<i>H-Huh? What just... What's the matter?</i>

04:21.860 --> 04:24.500
<i>Ah, okay. I see what's happening here.</i>

04:32.980 --> 04:34.920
That's not twue, Mister Les.

04:34.920 --> 04:37.470
Uwaz isn't selfish.

04:37.740 --> 04:38.450
What?

04:38.720 --> 04:40.340
He's the leader of the herd,

04:40.340 --> 04:43.350
so he doesn't like anyone he
doesn't know getting close.

04:43.350 --> 04:44.780
Right, Uwaz?

04:45.060 --> 04:48.080
Then... he acts like that on purpose

04:48.080 --> 04:50.400
so humans don't go near the herd?

04:50.630 --> 04:52.610
Horses do that?

04:52.610 --> 04:56.660
Well, Uwaz is a really smart boy.

05:02.830 --> 05:07.390
Is that so, Uwaz? I'm sorry 
I didn't realize it sooner.

05:17.000 --> 05:18.710
I see you two mounted up okay.

05:19.030 --> 05:20.670
That horse's name is Hugh.

05:20.670 --> 05:23.750
He's very docile and will go
 wherever you lead him,

05:23.750 --> 05:26.620
so he's perfect for inexperienced riders.

05:27.640 --> 05:31.050
<i>I wonder if this is the kind of white horse
fairy tale princes ride!</i>

05:34.180 --> 05:36.410
<i>He'd be perfect for my brother.</i>

05:36.410 --> 05:37.770
All right, let's go.

05:38.410 --> 05:40.460
The beast stables are quite large.

05:51.700 --> 05:53.650
What are they doing?

05:53.870 --> 05:55.800
That's a giant boar.

05:55.800 --> 05:59.380
They're looking for bugs to eat underground.

05:59.640 --> 06:01.540
<i>Ah, so it's lunchtime.</i>

06:07.100 --> 06:07.730
<i>Wha...</i>

06:08.390 --> 06:10.600
<i>What the?!</i>

06:10.600 --> 06:13.390
Er, looks like they've spotted us...

06:13.390 --> 06:17.310
Baby giant boars want someone to play with, 
so they'll charge at you.

06:17.690 --> 06:20.570
A number of beast knights 
get injured every year.

06:20.570 --> 06:22.280
What?! Really?!

06:22.760 --> 06:24.720
Help me!

06:40.380 --> 06:41.930
You saved us, Uwaz.

06:42.330 --> 06:43.990
Thank you, Uwaz!

06:53.330 --> 06:55.770
Over there, you can see a flock of wakkas.

06:56.460 --> 06:58.730
They are the fastest animals on land.

06:59.190 --> 07:02.190
Here, we use them as messengers
 and in emergencies.

07:02.500 --> 07:04.160
<i>The fastest animals on land?</i>

07:04.500 --> 07:06.210
I wanna ride one!

07:06.210 --> 07:07.240
Saw that coming...

07:07.770 --> 07:12.360
I'm afraid you need a great deal of training
to handle the wakkas' speed.

07:12.360 --> 07:14.570
Wanna ride! I wanna ride one!

07:14.570 --> 07:16.150
Very well, then.

07:17.270 --> 07:18.730
If we're both going to ride one,

07:18.730 --> 07:21.180
let's go with Yoshu here.
 He's quite energetic.

07:23.070 --> 07:25.330
Does your safety rope feel too tight?

07:25.910 --> 07:30.660
When you hold on to Yoshu, 
lean forward and hug him.

07:30.660 --> 07:32.430
<i>Can't... reach...</i>

07:32.880 --> 07:34.390
A little lower.

07:34.850 --> 07:37.340
So smooth! That feels nice!

07:37.610 --> 07:40.940
If you grab too hard, he'll stop,
 so please be careful.

07:41.200 --> 07:43.840
Yay! I'm so excited now!

07:43.840 --> 07:46.070
I wonder how fast he'll go!

07:46.070 --> 07:48.140
He's very, very fast.

07:48.480 --> 07:51.120
Mister Yoshu, pwease go as fast as you can!

07:51.560 --> 07:54.060
<i>I really mean it when I say he's fast.</i>

07:54.060 --> 07:56.590
<i>I can't believe she's not
 scared in the slightest.</i>

07:56.590 --> 07:57.850
All right, here we go.

08:05.330 --> 08:07.240
<i>What's with this speed?!</i>

08:07.240 --> 08:10.830
<i>It really hurts! I can't breathe!</i>

08:17.070 --> 08:19.650
Block the wind flow and make it fade.

08:23.540 --> 08:26.490
Huh? The wind's gone?

08:27.310 --> 08:28.840
I'm terribly sorry.

08:28.840 --> 08:31.600
I accidentally forgot to cast the spell.

08:32.790 --> 08:35.260
<i>Are you </i>sure<i> it was an accident?!</i>

08:35.260 --> 08:36.590
Please hold on.

08:36.590 --> 08:37.110
Huh?

08:37.450 --> 08:39.330
We're going to speed up a bit.

08:52.120 --> 08:55.580
I weally wespect people who wide wakkas...

08:56.090 --> 08:59.760
That was about 50 percent of its top speed.

09:04.370 --> 09:07.080
You good? You can barely walk.

09:08.120 --> 09:09.600
It's not <i>that</i> funny!

09:26.670 --> 09:28.410
Wow!

09:28.710 --> 09:33.390
That's a gleyhawk. 
We use them to exchange letters.

09:33.390 --> 09:34.760
<i>No fair...</i>

09:34.760 --> 09:39.230
<i>I want one on my arm, too. But I guess 
it's out of the question in this body.</i>

09:42.790 --> 09:43.650
Ah...

09:47.150 --> 09:47.770
Wha—

09:48.140 --> 09:51.800
I'm terribly sorry. One of my subordinates 
has caused some trouble.

09:51.800 --> 09:53.620
I must get back immediately.

09:53.900 --> 09:56.860
Got it. Guess we'll call it a day, then.

09:56.860 --> 10:00.440
Aw... Can we come back and play really soon?

10:00.810 --> 10:04.830
Yes. If I'm free, 
I'll be happy to show you around.

10:05.220 --> 10:08.030
<i>When the captain's free, huh?</i>

10:08.030 --> 10:09.950
<i>Well, so much for today.</i>

10:10.400 --> 10:12.840
Mister Dan, let's go see Ghizel!

10:12.840 --> 10:14.210
Right now?!

10:16.920 --> 10:21.130
What do you mean a white moose escaped?

10:21.470 --> 10:24.100
Of course it had to be a rare breed...

10:24.380 --> 10:26.130
I'm terribly sorry, sir!

10:26.130 --> 10:28.300
We're going to form a plan immediately.

10:28.690 --> 10:33.740
We will track it down with hounds and then,
 before it can put its guard up,

10:33.740 --> 10:35.520
we're going to capture it together.

10:35.520 --> 10:36.620
Yes, sir!

10:38.920 --> 10:41.730
Honestly, what were they even thinking?

10:43.240 --> 10:46.070
<i>Today's been one unpleasant
 thing after another.</i>

10:47.030 --> 10:49.380
<i>Of course, that includes the moose escaping,</i>

10:50.030 --> 10:52.990
<i>but also Uwaz taking a liking 
to Lady Nefertima...</i>

10:54.200 --> 10:57.340
<i>and then Yoshu obediently obeying orders.</i>

11:00.800 --> 11:03.300
Anyway, right now, the white 
moose takes precedence.

11:08.330 --> 11:09.440
Seriously...

11:09.850 --> 11:12.020
How in the world did this happen?!

11:12.280 --> 11:17.980
Lessee... I was twying to get back from 
visiting Ghizel, and she seemed lost.

11:18.260 --> 11:21.530
So you found her, Lady Nefertima?

11:21.530 --> 11:25.330
Nuh-uh. The elemental spiwits noticed 
she was lost and protected her.

11:25.690 --> 11:28.550
Then Lars told me, so we went and found her.

11:30.580 --> 11:33.500
<i>To think she'd also find the white moose...</i>

11:33.820 --> 11:36.890
<i>I underestimated Lady Nefertima.</i>

11:37.890 --> 11:42.550
From now on, if something like this happens 
again, could you contact us first?

11:43.030 --> 11:44.000
Okay!

11:44.350 --> 11:47.470
<i>The power to be loved by 
any kind of animal...</i>

11:47.470 --> 11:51.010
<i>I never thought such a thing existed,</i>

11:51.480 --> 11:53.510
<i>yet I have no choice but to accept it now.</i>

11:53.920 --> 11:55.780
<i>I'm rather jealous.</i>

11:55.780 --> 11:58.180
So warm!

11:55.780 --> 11:59.530
<i>I'd love that power myself, 
as I also adore animals.</i>

12:05.340 --> 12:07.980
Neema, happy birthday.

12:07.980 --> 12:09.940
Thank you very much!

12:09.940 --> 12:12.970
To celebrate your birthday, 
we'll grant you one wish.

12:12.970 --> 12:13.960
What would you like?

12:13.960 --> 12:15.570
Hmm...

12:16.260 --> 12:17.910
I wanna go to the city!

12:17.910 --> 12:21.100
Wha— N-No, absolutely not! It's dangerous!

12:21.100 --> 12:24.490
Dear, she'll be fine as long as
 she's with someone.

12:24.490 --> 12:25.460
I'll go with Karna!

12:25.700 --> 12:28.420
You girls going alone is just as bad!

12:28.710 --> 12:31.390
Then we'll just send Paul with them.

12:32.470 --> 12:35.490
S-So be it. I suppose I can accept that.

12:35.490 --> 12:36.590
Yay!

12:37.930 --> 12:42.260
Isn't that great, honey?
 Now let's get you ready for your outing.

12:42.260 --> 12:42.900
Okay!

12:43.120 --> 12:46.790
<i>Hooray! My first shopping trip!</i>

12:51.550 --> 12:53.200
Wow! It's so lively here.

12:53.590 --> 12:55.800
Well, this is the commercial district.

12:56.270 --> 13:00.560
The royal capital is split 
into four distinct areas.

12:58.340 --> 12:59.570
Palace

12:59.130 --> 13:00.360
Noble District

12:59.560 --> 13:05.260
Palace

13:00.350 --> 13:02.510
Noble District

13:00.380 --> 13:02.090
Commercial District

13:01.630 --> 13:05.260
Industrial District
(Workshops & Schools)

13:01.810 --> 13:04.570
<i>Ah, it almost looks like a baumkuchen!</i>

13:02.090 --> 13:05.260
Commercial District

13:02.510 --> 13:05.260
Noble District

13:02.880 --> 13:05.260
Common District

13:05.450 --> 13:10.630
Apparently, the first king wanted the city 
to look beautiful even from the sky.

13:11.670 --> 13:15.290
I'm so happy that I get to go 
shopping with you, Neema!

13:15.290 --> 13:16.910
So let's get to it!

13:17.380 --> 13:19.600
W-Wait for me!

13:24.550 --> 13:25.720
Step right up!

13:26.370 --> 13:27.920
<i>It's like a street festival!</i>

13:27.920 --> 13:29.020
<i>It looks so fun!</i>

13:33.470 --> 13:36.940
Hey, hey! Can you teach me how to use money?

13:36.940 --> 13:38.030
Sure.

13:39.020 --> 13:41.010
The smallest unit of currency is a rye.

13:41.900 --> 13:44.720
Ten ryes are equal to one copper ingot.

13:44.990 --> 13:47.780
The drinks at that stall cost eight ryes.

13:48.040 --> 13:52.760
Enjoying drinks at a café will probably
cost you around three copper ingots.

13:53.260 --> 13:54.580
<i>I see...</i>

13:54.580 --> 13:57.980
<i>Okay, I think I got it down. Time to shop!</i>

13:59.530 --> 14:01.150
I'd like three, pwease.

14:01.480 --> 14:04.540
Oh? You've got good taste, little lady!

14:04.540 --> 14:07.120
We've got the world's most 
delicious turkey here.

14:07.540 --> 14:09.700
<i>Yeah, this is it!</i>

14:09.950 --> 14:11.910
Three legs will be three copper ingots.

14:12.310 --> 14:15.050
One... two... three.

14:16.120 --> 14:16.890
Here!

14:17.820 --> 14:19.820
Be careful. They're hot.

14:19.820 --> 14:20.830
Okay!

14:21.760 --> 14:24.780
<i>My first shopping trip was a success!</i>

14:25.810 --> 14:27.030
Karna!

14:27.710 --> 14:28.720
Here you go!

14:30.630 --> 14:31.550
Thanks.

14:31.890 --> 14:33.120
You too, Paul!

14:33.120 --> 14:35.260
What? But I'm on the clock...

14:35.510 --> 14:38.360
I'm trying to bribe you 
into holding my stuff.

14:40.090 --> 14:41.560
Thank you very much.

14:41.800 --> 14:43.420
Here, Dee.

14:43.420 --> 14:46.900
Just for today, though. 
It's my birthday, so you get a special treat.

14:49.730 --> 14:52.150
The bone can be dangerous, so allow me.

14:52.150 --> 14:53.340
Thanks!

14:54.340 --> 14:55.860
<i>Hmm? I wonder what that is.</i>

14:56.350 --> 14:59.790
<i>Now I smell something nice and sweet...</i>

15:05.760 --> 15:07.170
Wh-What's that?!

15:07.570 --> 15:09.430
It's a confection called pepe.

15:09.430 --> 15:12.780
When they fry the boiled dough,
 it puffs up like that.

15:13.490 --> 15:15.560
I-I'mma go buy some!

15:16.480 --> 15:17.670
I'd like three, pwease!

15:18.080 --> 15:20.310
My, what a cute little girl.

15:20.310 --> 15:21.850
Will three be enough?

15:21.850 --> 15:25.260
If you buy twenty, 
I'll throw in an extra three.

15:25.590 --> 15:28.760
<i>Twenty?! How many are you 
trying to get me to buy, lady?!</i>

15:28.760 --> 15:30.120
<i>Oh, but...</i>

15:30.410 --> 15:32.830
Could you make it four, pwease?

15:32.830 --> 15:33.820
Sure thing.

15:34.510 --> 15:36.810
I wanna give one to Dee, too!

15:37.340 --> 15:40.260
Oh my. You two must be close.

15:40.260 --> 15:44.520
All right. For twenty and four, 
that'll be one copper coin.

15:44.520 --> 15:45.370
<i>So cheap!</i>

15:46.250 --> 15:49.120
Heave-ho, heave-ho...

15:48.160 --> 15:49.720
Neema! Neema!

15:50.470 --> 15:52.770
What are you going to do with all of that?

15:53.300 --> 15:59.270
Well, I bought some for Mama and Papa
 and everyone at home!

16:01.950 --> 16:05.200
You're... You're...

16:05.640 --> 16:07.650
Such a sweet little girl!

16:08.050 --> 16:10.810
Goodness! You're so adorable!

16:10.820 --> 16:12.110
I can't bweathe...

16:12.510 --> 16:14.390
L-Lady Karna...

16:14.390 --> 16:17.020
You're going to crush both 
Lady Neema and the pepes.

16:17.670 --> 16:20.090
O-Oh, sorry.

16:23.140 --> 16:25.590
Neema, why don't we stop by this place?

16:25.590 --> 16:27.920
I come here all the time. I just love it.

16:30.990 --> 16:34.100
My, Lady Karnadia.
How do you do this fine day?

16:34.390 --> 16:35.170
Ack...

16:35.810 --> 16:37.630
<i>Did she just say, "Ack"?</i>

16:37.630 --> 16:38.820
Good day to you.

16:38.820 --> 16:43.550
It's quite rare for us to bump 
into each other here.

16:43.550 --> 16:46.150
I was just shopping with my sister.

16:47.310 --> 16:49.240
Ah, the one I keep hearing about.

16:49.570 --> 16:51.190
<i>Huh? She's heard of me?</i>

16:51.450 --> 16:54.790
It must be hard having such 
a failure for a sister.

16:54.790 --> 16:55.530
<i>Wha—?!</i>

16:55.530 --> 16:58.900
She has no magical power and 
doesn't even look like your parents.

16:58.900 --> 17:01.390
Not to mention those creepy black eyes...

17:01.390 --> 17:04.500
How could she possibly be a noble?

17:09.380 --> 17:13.160
I see none of you can appreciate
 how wonderful my sister is.

17:14.080 --> 17:17.340
Anyone who's clever can tell immediately.

17:17.610 --> 17:19.550
And what do you mean by that?!

17:19.550 --> 17:25.370
I'm talking about the people who see
just how incredible my little sister is.

17:25.750 --> 17:26.300
Like, say...

17:26.620 --> 17:28.520
The royal family.

17:33.700 --> 17:40.200
Belittling someone you've just met 
is most unbecoming for a noblewoman.

17:40.670 --> 17:45.440
I'd be sullying my good family's name 
to associate with someone like you.

17:46.660 --> 17:47.870
Let's go home.

17:49.260 --> 17:51.200
Okay, Karna!

17:51.930 --> 17:53.930
Have a lovely day, ladies.

18:01.280 --> 18:03.420
Neema, you must be tired.

18:03.420 --> 18:05.630
I slept in the carriage, so I'm fine.

18:05.880 --> 18:08.150
<i>Man, that was so much fun.</i>

18:08.150 --> 18:13.140
<i>Those people we ran into at the café
were annoying, but my sister was so cool.</i>

18:13.140 --> 18:14.930
<i>What a great birthday.</i>

18:19.810 --> 18:22.340
Happy birthday, Neema!

18:23.110 --> 18:25.920
Happy birthday! Happy birthday!

18:28.570 --> 18:31.330
We kept this a secret 
so we could surprise you.

18:32.050 --> 18:34.930
<i>Huh? Everyone's so busy...</i>

18:35.320 --> 18:38.850
<i>But they all got together
 to prepare this for me?</i>

18:39.590 --> 18:41.650
Looks like it was a big success.

18:41.650 --> 18:44.220
The adorable little princess 
is clearly surprised.

18:47.890 --> 18:51.050
Fank you sho much...

18:51.050 --> 18:54.410
Oh no. We made the little princess cry.

18:54.740 --> 18:56.880
She just must be that happy.

19:00.230 --> 19:02.080
You sure do look ugly when you cry.

19:02.420 --> 19:04.300
You shut up!

19:06.210 --> 19:08.710
All right, let's eat.

19:10.040 --> 19:13.180
To Nefertima growing up healthy!

19:13.570 --> 19:14.840
Cheers!

19:18.130 --> 19:20.140
Neema, come here.

19:22.560 --> 19:25.640
This is a gift from the king and myself.

19:29.350 --> 19:31.570
It's a necklace with magical stones.

19:31.570 --> 19:34.470
I've included some very powerful ones.

19:34.770 --> 19:38.010
You need a certain spell to use this.

19:38.010 --> 19:38.940
A spell?

19:38.940 --> 19:42.330
The magical chant is "Help me, Uncle Gauldi!"

19:43.110 --> 19:44.030
Goodness.

19:44.340 --> 19:47.380
What nonsense are you going on about, Father?

19:51.830 --> 19:53.410
Here. This is from me.

19:53.750 --> 19:57.430
Unlike the gift from my mother
 and father, it'll protect you.

19:57.890 --> 19:59.710
Make sure you always keep it on you.

19:59.960 --> 20:03.930
<i>So he's basically saying what 
they gave me is useless?</i>

20:04.370 --> 20:07.270
I got you clothes, a hat, and some shoes!

20:07.270 --> 20:10.380
They've been altered so you can 
wear them when you're bigger.

20:10.870 --> 20:12.600
Here's a blade to protect you.

20:12.920 --> 20:15.750
An encyclopedia of the animals in all regions.

20:15.750 --> 20:17.560
From the imperial guard.

20:17.960 --> 20:21.570
This is a hair clip made from the scales 
of dragons at the stables.

20:21.570 --> 20:24.330
Neck scales, even. They're the hardest.

20:24.330 --> 20:27.410
The dragons cooperated
 when I collected them, too.

20:27.710 --> 20:31.100
<i>Scales from the place 
they hate being touched the most?!</i>

20:32.250 --> 20:35.620
<i>The next time I see them, I'm going 
to give them so many head pats!</i>

20:35.950 --> 20:37.710
And this is from me.

20:39.220 --> 20:42.700
This little one is related to the 
gleyhawk. It's called a rain hawk.

20:42.700 --> 20:47.250
She's the cleverest and strongest 
that was born this earth season.

20:49.030 --> 20:49.840
Cheep.

20:49.840 --> 20:51.920
<i>She's so fluffy!</i>

20:51.920 --> 20:53.070
I can keep her?

20:53.290 --> 20:59.270
We raised her to grow up indoors,
and your parents gave their blessing.

21:00.340 --> 21:04.940
You were looking so intently 
at the gleyhawk the other day.

21:05.750 --> 21:11.640
Gleyhawks are far too big for you still, 
so please take care of this rain hawk instead.

21:20.670 --> 21:23.590
<b>Remember to study.</b>

21:24.220 --> 21:27.170
Thank you very much, everyone!

21:27.170 --> 21:29.590
This was the best birthday ever!

21:36.360 --> 21:38.710
<i>Today was so much fun.</i>

21:38.710 --> 21:41.320
<i>So many people came to celebrate my birthday.</i>

21:41.320 --> 21:42.260
Cheep.

21:43.390 --> 21:46.310
Oh, yeah. I haven't given you a name yet.

21:46.310 --> 21:48.950
Hmm... What should I call you?

21:48.950 --> 21:50.530
Cheep... Cheep?

21:51.830 --> 21:52.870
Nox.

21:53.350 --> 21:55.190
From now on, you're Nox.

21:55.190 --> 21:55.810
Cheep!

21:56.380 --> 21:59.090
Let's be great fwiends, Nox!

23:35.180 --> 23:40.050
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.180 --> 23:40.050
<b>I Hate Studying!</b>
